+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup — **blocks every user story**
+- **User Stories (Phases 3–6)**: All depend on Foundational completion
+- **Polish (Phase 7)**: T034 and T038 depend on all four stories; T035 depends on US1 and US3;
+  T036, T037, T039 and T040 depend on everything desired being complete
+
+### User Story Dependencies
+
+- **US1 (P1)**: Depends only on Foundational. No dependency on another story — this is the MVP
+- **US2 (P2)**: Depends on Foundational. Reuses `normalise_tags` (T014), `list_bookmarks` (T017)
+  and the TSV renderer (T018) from US1, so in practice it follows US1; it remains independently
+  testable because its tests seed the store through `add`
+- **US3 (P3)**: Depends on Foundational. Needs `add`/`list` from US1 to be observable
+- **US4 (P3)**: Depends on Foundational. Reuses `list_bookmarks` from US1; independent of US2
+  and US3
+
+US2, US3 and US4 do not depend on each other and can proceed in any order or in parallel once US1
+is done.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written first and must FAIL before the implementation tasks begin
+- `store.py` data rules before `cli.py` presentation
+- Subparser registration last, since it wires an already-working handler into the grammar
+- The story's checkpoint is reached only when its own tests pass
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- T007 (`cli.py` parser skeleton) runs in parallel with T004–T006 (`store.py`) — different files
+- T010 (`tests/conftest.py`) runs in parallel with all of T004–T009
+- T012 (`tests/test_add.py`) and T013 (`tests/test_list_search.py`) run in parallel
+- T022 is **not** parallel with T013 — both edit `tests/test_list_search.py`
+- T014–T020 are strictly sequential: T014–T017 all edit `store.py`, T018–T020 all edit `cli.py`
+- T027 (US3 tests) and T030 (US4 tests) run in parallel with each other and with US2 work
+- T034, T035 and T037 run in parallel — three different files, and T037 touches none
+- Once Foundational is done, US2, US3 and US4 can be staffed to different people in parallel
