+## Implementation Strategy
+
+### MVP First (User Story 1 Only)
+
+1. Complete Phase 1: Setup (T001–T003)
+2. Complete Phase 2: Foundational (T004–T011) — **blocks everything**
+3. Complete Phase 3: User Story 1 (T012–T021)
+4. **STOP and VALIDATE**: run quickstart scenarios 1, 2, 7 and 8; `pytest` green
+5. A tool that captures and reviews bookmarks is deliverable here
+
+### Incremental Delivery
+
+1. Setup + Foundational → store lifecycle and entry point proven
+2. Add US1 → test independently → **MVP** (add + list)
+3. Add US2 → test independently → retrieval at scale (`--tag`, `search`)
+4. Add US3 → test independently → pruning, with identifiers retired
+5. Add US4 → test independently → portability (CSV, JSON)
+6. Polish → contract-wide statuses and streams, performance budget, quality gates
+
+Each story adds value without breaking the previous ones.
+
+### Parallel Team Strategy
+
+1. The team completes Setup + Foundational together — it is the only truly blocking work
+2. One person then takes US1, which US2–US4 build on in practice
+3. Once US1 lands: Developer A on US2, Developer B on US3, Developer C on US4 — three disjoint
+   store functions and three disjoint subparsers, with only `cli.py` as a shared file to
+   coordinate on
+4. Polish is done once, by whoever lands last
