+## Notes
+
+- **Tests are mandatory here, not optional** — FR-027 and Principle III (NON-NEGOTIABLE). Each
+  test names the requirement it covers, in its name or a comment
+- Exit statuses and the stdout/stderr split are asserted by invoking the CLI as a **subprocess**;
+  an in-process call cannot observe a real process exit status
+- The status map is complete and exhaustive: 0 success, 1 unusable store, 2 any user mistake,
+  3 deleting an identifier that does not exist. Status 3 is reserved **exclusively** for the
+  well-formed-but-absent identifier — never for `delete abc`
+- Four of the five usage-mistake cases fall out of the argparse declaration (`required=True`,
+  positionals, `type=int`, `choices`). Writing validation code for them would be the scope
+  Principle IV calls a defect
+- `AUTOINCREMENT`, `PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON`, `lineterminator="\n"`, `newline=""`,
+  `ensure_ascii=False` and `prog="python -m bookmarks"` are each load-bearing for a specific
+  requirement — none is decoration, and removing any one silently breaks a requirement
+- [P] tasks = different files, no dependencies. Tasks editing `store.py` or `cli.py` are never [P]
+  with each other
+- Commit after each task or logical group; stop at any checkpoint to validate a story
+  independently